WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.070
Here's a fruit fly with legs growing
where its antennae should be.

2
00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:06.950
And here's one with a
second pair of wings.

3
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.360
Mutations can turn one
body part into another.

4
00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:16.010
Yet every fly begins as a zygote,
dividing into a ball of identical cells.

5
00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:21.010
So how does a ball of identical cells
know where to build a head and a tail?

6
00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:24.910
In this mission, you'll meet the
genes that set up body plans.

7
00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:27.420
They code for transcription factors.

8
00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:30.270
Then you'll test your idea on a new case:

9
00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:32.840
digits forming in a growing limb.

10
00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:37.970
Your mission: explain how a ball of
identical cells knows where to build a head

11
00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:38.840
and a tail.
